@namespace NoBorders.Components.Screens
@* Screen 1g's toast, design-handoff/README.md §"1g".
   Phase 6.2: this is now the live root component of a small, dedicated,
   always-on-top BlazorWebView window (see MainForm.ShowToast) — the
   Adaptation Decision made for this item was a separate host window
   matching the old GDI ShowToast's independent screen-corner positioning,
   not a docked overlay inside MainForm's own BlazorWebView. This window
   IS the toast (no page chrome around it), so — unlike other screens —
   there's no outer positioning here; the host Form is sized/placed by
   WinForms exactly as the old GDI popup was, and this component just
   fills it.

   Progress bar: a single CSS animation (nb-toast-countdown, 6s linear)
   rather than a C#-driven percentage, since "auto-dismiss ~6s along the
   progress bar" (README, Interactions & Behavior) is a fixed duration,
   not live data — no need for repeated Blazor re-renders just to tick a
   number down. MainForm's own auto-close timer uses a matching duration
   so the window disappears right as the bar visually empties.

   Undo intentionally omitted (ShowUndo defaults false, and MainForm never
   passes true): the README's Interactions text describes toast Undo as
   reverting "the applied bounds," but none of ShowToast's real call sites
   (add/refresh/elevation-warning) capture an undo snapshot the way
   BtnSaveGame_Click does (Phase 4.13) — wiring a live "Undo" link to
   nothing would be a dead click target on a real, user-facing popup,
   worse than the mock's static screenshot. Left in the markup, gated
   behind the parameter, for whenever a real snapshot exists to revert to. *@

<div class="nb-toast @(Success ? "" : "nb-toast--danger")">
    <div class="nb-toast__row">
        <div class="nb-toast__thumb" style="@ThumbStyle"></div>
        <div class="nb-toast__body">
            <div class="nb-toast__status">
                <span class="nb-toast__dot"></span>
                <span class="nb-toast__title">@Title</span>
            </div>
            <div class="nb-toast__detail">@Detail</div>
            @if (ShowUndo)
            {
                <div class="nb-toast__undo nb-mono">Undo · Ctrl+Shift+Z</div>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="nb-toast__progress-track">
        <div class="nb-toast__progress-fill"></div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Title { get; set; } = "Borderless applied";
    [Parameter] public string Detail { get; set; } = "Helldivers 2 → 2560×1440 on LG 27GP850";
    [Parameter] public bool Success { get; set; } = true;
    [Parameter] public bool ShowUndo { get; set; } = false;

    // Phase 8.3: the toast's own game, if any (hotkey-conflict/elevation
    // toasts have none) — empty means "no cached icon yet," leaving the
    // existing placeholder background-image rule showing through.
    [Parameter] public string IconUrl { get; set; } = "";

    private string ThumbStyle =>
        string.IsNullOrEmpty(IconUrl) ? "" : $"background-image:url('{IconUrl}');background-size:cover;background-position:center;";
}
